Build a complete, futuristic, interactive science website called SciVerse — The Ultimate Interactive Science Universe.

PROJECT VISION:
Create a visually stunning, educational, interactive science platform where people can explore how the universe works. Combine the feel of a futuristic laboratory, NASA-style space exploration centre, engineering simulator, chemistry laboratory, physics playground and science video game. The website should make science exciting by letting users interact with scientific concepts, experiment in safe virtual environments, explore simulations, change variables and immediately see what happens.

The website must be a real, functioning product rather than just a static landing page. Implement working navigation, simulations, interactive controls, searchable science topics, quizzes, learning tools and responsive layouts wherever supported. Do not leave important buttons nonfunctional or fill the website with placeholder text.

BRAND AND VISUAL IDENTITY:
Use the name SciVerse. Create a memorable logo combining an atom, orbit and small star, with subtle motion. Use a premium futuristic visual style with deep navy and near-black backgrounds, electric cyan, bright blue, violet and small accents of orange for heat, combustion and energy. Use glowing outlines sparingly, glass-like panels, fine grid lines, scientific diagrams, cinematic space backgrounds, smooth animations and high-quality 3D-style illustrations. Use clear typography, large but readable headings, comfortable spacing and strong contrast. The result should feel sophisticated, immersive and professional, not cluttered or childish.

Support a dark theme as the main experience and a light theme as an option. Use responsive layouts for desktop, tablets and mobile. Prioritise performance, accessible controls and reduced-motion preferences.

HOMEPAGE:
Create an impressive homepage with a large animated galaxy or scientific laboratory background, floating particles, orbiting planets and subtle molecular animations. Display the headline “Explore Everything. Understand Anything.” and supporting text explaining that users can discover science through interactive experiments and simulations.

Include prominent buttons for “Enter the Lab”, “Explore the Universe” and “Start Experimenting”. Each button must lead to its proper working page or interactive experience.

Add an interactive universe of science categories, displayed as attractive cards:
1. Chemistry and Chemical Reactions
2. Physics and Speed
3. Water and Fluid Dynamics
4. Wind and Weather
5. Space and Astronomy
6. Rockets and Spacecraft
7. Combustion and Energy
